---
import RecordCard from './RecordCard.astro';

const requestFields = [
  { label: 'Licence', value: 'LIC-4471' },
  { label: 'Requested change', value: 'Correct recorded activities' },
  { label: 'Submitted by', value: 'Licence holder' },
  { label: 'Received', value: 'Tuesday 09:14' },
];
const licenceFields = [
  { label: 'Permitted activities', value: 'Corrected' },
  { label: 'Changed by', value: 'Licensing application' },
  { label: 'Applied', value: 'Wednesday 10:02' },
  { label: 'Revision', value: '12' },
];
---

<figure class="casework-flow" aria-labelledby="casework-flow-title">
  <div class="flow-intro">
    <p class="flow-kicker">An illustrative correction request</p>
    <h3 id="casework-flow-title">Staff review the request. The licensing application updates the professional register after approval.</h3>
  </div>

  <div class="work-journey" role="group" aria-label="Fictional licence correction moving from request to inbox to applied change">
    <section class="request-panel" aria-labelledby="request-panel-title">
      <div class="panel-heading">
        <p class="panel-label">Licensing application</p>
        <h4 id="request-panel-title">Correction request</h4>
      </div>
      <RecordCard recordType="Correction request" recordId="REQ-3106" icon="data" fields={requestFields} />
      <p class="panel-note">The licensing application collects the request and supporting documents.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="inbox-panel" aria-labelledby="inbox-panel-title">
      <div class="panel-heading">
        <p class="panel-label">Registry Casework</p>
        <h4 id="inbox-panel-title">Licence correction reviews</h4>
      </div>
      <ol class="item-history">
        <li><strong>Request sent for review</strong><span>The request enters the licence corrections queue with a due date.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Missing certificate identified</strong><span>The reviewer asks for the certificate. This completes the first review.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Certificate provided</strong><span>The licensing application collects the certificate and submits a new review request.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Revised request approved</strong><span>A reviewer records the approval. This review has its own due date.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="panel-note">Supervisors can see who is responsible for each review and when it is due.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="register-panel" aria-labelledby="register-panel-title">
      <div class="panel-heading">
        <p class="panel-label">Professional register</p>
        <h4 id="register-panel-title">Change applied</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="applied-record">
        <p class="applied-label"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Updated by the licensing application</p>
        <RecordCard recordType="Licence record" recordId="LIC-4471" icon="person" fields={licenceFields} />
      </div>
      <p class="panel-note">The licensing application asks the professional register to apply the approved correction. The register checks permission before accepting the change.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="audit-slip">
      <svg class="audit-mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M6 3h12v18H6zM9 7h6M9 11h6M9 15h4" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>Review history</strong> When each review was submitted, assigned and completed, and who made the decision. The register keeps the history of record changes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>Fictional licence data. In this example, the licensing application submits the approved correction to the professional register. Registry Casework records each staff review.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .casework-flow { margin: 0 auto; max-width: var(--registry-max); }
  .flow-intro { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); margin-bottom: 25px; padding-bottom: 20px; }
  .flow-intro h3 { font-size: var(--type-subhead); line-height: 1.4; margin: 7px 0 0; }
  .flow-kicker, .panel-label { color: var(--registry-blue); font: var(--type-2xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono); margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .work-journey { align-items: start; display: grid; gap: 24px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .request-panel, .inbox-panel, .register-panel { min-width: 0; }
  .panel-heading { margin-bottom: 13px; }
  .panel-heading h4 { font-size: var(--type-subhead); line-height: 1.3; margin: 5px 0 0; }
  .panel-note { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-sm); line-height: 1.5; margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .item-history { background: var(--registry-slate-tint); border: 1px solid var(--registry-slate-rule); display: grid; gap: 14px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 16px 18px; }
  .item-history li { border-left: 2px solid var(--registry-blue); display: grid; gap: 3px; padding-left: 12px; }
  .item-history strong { color: var(--registry-ink); font-size: var(--type-base); line-height: 1.4; }
  .item-history span { color: var(--registry-body); font-size: var(--type-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
  .applied-record { background: var(--registry-blue-tint); padding: 0 10px 10px; }
  .applied-label { align-items: center; color: var(--registry-blue); display: flex; gap: 8px; font: var(--type-2xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono); margin: 0; padding: 10px 5px; }
  .applied-label > span { font-size: var(--type-body); }
  .audit-slip { align-items: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); display: flex; gap: 12px; grid-column: 1 / -1; padding-top: 18px; }
  .audit-mark { color: var(--registry-blue); flex: 0 0 auto; height: 25px; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.5; width: 25px; }
  .audit-slip p { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-sm); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
  .audit-slip strong { color: var(--registry-body); font-weight: 600; margin-right: 8px; }
  .casework-flow figcaption { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-xs); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .work-journey { gap: 20px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .audit-slip { align-items: start; }
  }
</style>
